    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0059" n="52" xml:id="pg52"/>

                <head>No. 38.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McAdoo to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-04-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                    1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith, for
                    your information, copies of a communication from Capt. J. C. Watson, U. S. N.,
                    commanding the II. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">San Francisco</hi>, dated
                    Bluefields, Nicaragua, April 16, with eighteen inclosures, reporting on the
                    state of affairs in the Mosquito Reservation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. McAdoo</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of the Navy.</hi></signed></closer>























